<title>UK: NWE oil output steady at 6.323 mbpd in Jan - WoodMac.</title>
<headline>NWE oil output steady at 6.323 mbpd in Jan - WoodMac.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northwest European (NWE) oil output in January was steady at 6.323 million barrels a day (bpd) just 13,000 bpd below December's 6.336 million, consultancy Wood Mackenzie said.</p>
<p>Slightly higher Norwegian production just failed to compensate for a fall from the British North Sea sector.</p>
<p>Norway pumped 3.389 million bpd from 3.338 million in December.</p>
<p>Britain produced 2.669 million in January versus 2.731 million, including just over 110,000 bpd from onshore fields.</p>
<p>Danish output was 228,000 bpd from 232,000 bpd in December.</p>
<p>The Netherlands supplied 36,000 bpd from 35,000 bpd.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
